NOTE ON DATA — THIS REPOSITORY IS DUAL LICENSED.

The MIT license above covers CODE ONLY.

Benchmark ITEMS are licensed separately, per item, according to the source they
derive from. Every item carries a `license` field recording its terms.

In particular, items derived from the Bangor Miami Corpus (TalkBank/BilingBank) are
licensed CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, per TalkBank's access-page terms for that corpus. Note: the
corpus's own depositor-authored documentation separately states GPL v3, and the two
public TalkBank pages have not been reconciled with each other (see docs/corpora.md §1).
This project complies with the union of both readings' obligations rather than picking
one, which in practice means:

  - NonCommercial. Those items may not be used in commercial products.
  - ShareAlike / no relicensing. Adaptations must carry an equivalent obligation.
  - Attribution. Cite Deuchar, M., & Parafita Couto, M. (2011). The Bangor Miami
    Corpus. TalkBank. doi:10.21415/T5J01D

Whether a model fine-tuned on these items constitutes a GPL "derivative work" is a
separate, unresolved question this project has not chased down (see docs/corpora.md §1).
If your use case turns on that question, verify it independently.

If you need MIT-only material, filter items by their `license` field. Do not
assume the MIT grant above extends to any item.

See docs/corpora.md for the full licensing analysis.
